From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicolas Villar <15879262+nvillar@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 11:43:59 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Duo: Back at the root of a panel task minimizes it instead of
 doing nothing

Back at the root of an app started from home (ActivityClientController.onBackPressed with a MAIN/LAUNCHER base intent
launched from home) or an explicit Activity.moveTaskToBack moves the root task to the back of its task display area
(Task.moveTaskToBack -> moveToBack -> positionChildAt(POSITION_BOTTOM)). On a phone the task then sits behind home and
stops. A panel's task area (Panel0Tasks / Panel1Tasks) has no home: with one task in the panel nothing changed, the task
stayed on top of its panel, visible and resumed, and Back did nothing at all (gate G4.back: "no lifecycle change").

It also stranded predictive Back (ledger F22). A committed cross-task Back preview waits for the closing transition of
that Back (BackNavigationController.onTransactionReady sets mPrepareCloseTransition, and the composed animation is only
cleared when that transition finishes). The TO_BACK transition of a no-op moveTaskToBack has no targets, so it never
became the closing transition: Shell kept holding the prepare transition with mCloseTransitionRequested set, the
animation stayed composed, the closing task kept its 0.8 post-commit transform ([135,180][1215,1620] on panel 0) and
the opening target stayed paused for touch (WindowState.canReceiveTouchInput -> shouldPauseTouch), until the tasks
were removed; every later Back returned "Previous animation hasn't finish".

After moveToBack, the root task of the moved task (not the task moveTaskToBack was called on: an organizer-created root
leaves itself in place and reparents the task out of it), if it is in a panel task area, is hidden with the policy's
own reason, FLAG_FORCE_HIDDEN_FOR_DUO_PANEL, collected into the transition being collected (the TO_BACK, or the OPEN
it joins).
That is what Home does for a whole panel: the panel shows home (or its next task), the task stops, and the Back
transition now carries the closing task. It is shown again when it is moved to front (relaunch, Recents, a focus move:
restoreHiddenByPolicy, fw 0014). Other task display areas (the spanned default area) keep the platform behaviour.

Not built or run on a device yet. Verified by git am -3 after the series and a javac type check of the changed classes
against the gate build's framework and services jars.

Co-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../wm/DuoDisplayAreaPolicyProvider.java      | 22 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../core/java/com/android/server/wm/Task.java |  3 +++
 2 files changed, 25 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/DuoDisplayAreaPolicyProvider.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/DuoDisplayAreaPolicyProvider.java
index 73a4d40fb..db98daca4 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/DuoDisplayAreaPolicyProvider.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/DuoDisplayAreaPolicyProvider.java
@@ -213,6 +213,28 @@ public class DuoDisplayAreaPolicyProvider implements DisplayAreaPolicy.Provider
         return restored;
     }
 
+    /**
+     * Back at the root of an app started from home (ActivityClientController.onBackPressed) or an explicit
+     * moveTaskToBack moves the root task to the back of its task display area; on a phone it then sits behind home.
+     * A panel's task area has no home, so the task stayed on top of its panel, visible and resumed: Back did nothing,
+     * and a predictive Back preview committed on it never got its closing transition and stayed composed (the other
+     * panel's task paused for touch, ledger F22). Hides the task with the policy's own reason, as Home does for a
+     * whole panel, so that panel shows home (or its next task) and the task stops; it is shown again when it is moved
+     * to front (relaunch, Recents: {@link #restoreHiddenByPolicy}). A no-op outside a panel task area.
+     */
+    static void minimizeMovedToBack(Task rootTask) {
+        if (!sActive || rootTask == null || !rootTask.isRootTask()) return;
+        final TaskDisplayArea tda = rootTask.getDisplayArea();
+        if (tda == null || !(tda.getRootDisplayArea() instanceof PanelGroup)) return;
+        final TransitionController transitions = rootTask.mTransitionController;
+        if (transitions.isCollecting()) {
+            transitions.collect(rootTask);
+        }
+        if (rootTask.setForceHidden(Task.FLAG_FORCE_HIDDEN_FOR_DUO_PANEL, true /* set */)) {
+            Slog.i(TAG, "Back: minimized " + rootTask + " on " + tda.getRootDisplayArea().getName());
+        }
+    }
+
     /**
      * The panel a launch should go to, from where the user tapped. A launcher passes the on-screen rectangle of the
      * tapped icon as the intent's source bounds; the panel containing it gets the new task, so an icon on the left
diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/Task.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/Task.java
index 8fbcc924f..793933175 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/Task.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/Task.java
@@ -6043,6 +6043,9 @@ class Task extends TaskFragment {
         }
         try {
             moveToBack("moveTaskToBackInner", task);
+            // Duo two panel policy: a panel's task area has no home to go behind; hide the task as Home would. The root
+            // of the moved task: an organizer root leaves itself in place and reparents the task out of it.
+            DuoDisplayAreaPolicyProvider.minimizeMovedToBack(task.getRootTask());
 
             if (inPinnedWindowingMode()) {
                 mTaskSupervisor.removeRootTask(this);
